cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this research companion, cite it using the metadata below.
  This record describes the package, not an accepted or published journal article.
type: software
title: >-
  Linear Residual Boosting for Rotor-Temperature Estimation in
  Permanent-Magnet Synchronous Motors: Accuracy, Initialization,
  and Computational Cost
authors:
  - family-names: Jo
    given-names: Minsu
  - family-names: Yoo
    given-names: Namhyun
  - family-names: Kim
    given-names: Beomseok
  - family-names: Choi
    given-names: Hoansuk
  - family-names: Yang
    given-names: Jinhong
version: 0.4.0
date-released: '2026-11-17'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/JoMinsu-KU/pmsm-linear-residual-boosting'
abstract: >-
  Portable data preparation, model fitting, evaluation, scalar CPU benchmarking,
  and table and figure generation for permanent-magnet synchronous motor
  rotor-temperature estimation, with the v011 manuscript's six saved-data figure
  renderings, residual-correction, operating-range, and paired initialization
  analyses. The study compares linear residual boosting,
  direct boosting, averaging, initialization interventions, and neural controls
  using fixed previously selected settings. All configured evaluation profiles
  were historically exposed; a fresh execution is a computational reproduction,
  not independent confirmation. Complete raw datasets are acquired separately.
keywords:
  - filter initialization
  - gradient boosting
  - inference latency
  - permanent-magnet synchronous motor
  - residual learning
  - rotor temperature
